%% DFMS Trip State Diagram — Full 13-state lifecycle
%% Aligned with gate_entries status enum and DB schema
%% Last Updated: March 2026

stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Pending : Transport Order created

    %% ── Pre-departure ──────────────────────────────
    Pending --> Assigned : Vehicle + driver confirmed\n(TO dispatched)
    Pending --> Cancelled : Trip cancelled before dispatch

    Assigned --> GateIn : Vehicle arrives at origin gate\n(gate-in recorded by gate operator)
    Assigned --> OnHold : Pre-departure incident raised
    Assigned --> Cancelled : Trip cancelled after assignment

    %% ── Origin operations ──────────────────────────
    GateIn --> Loading : Gate operator starts loading\n(POST /operations/loading/start)

    Loading --> LoadingComplete : Quantity loaded confirmed\n(POST /operations/loading/complete)
    Loading --> OnHold : Loading incident raised

    LoadingComplete --> ScaleIn : Tare (empty) weight recorded\n(POST /operations/scale-in)
    LoadingComplete --> OnHold : Pre-departure hold

    %% ── In transit ─────────────────────────────────
    ScaleIn --> InTransit : Vehicle departs origin gate\n(driver confirms departure)
    InTransit --> InTransit : GPS location update\n(every 60 seconds)
    InTransit --> OnHold : Breakdown / incident en route\n(driver or supervisor action)

    %% ── Destination operations ─────────────────────
    InTransit --> GateOut : Vehicle arrives at destination gate\n(gate-out recorded by gate operator)

    GateOut --> Unloading : Gate operator starts unloading\n(POST /operations/unloading/start)
    GateOut --> OnHold : Destination hold

    Unloading --> ScaleOut : Gross weight recorded after unloading\n(POST /operations/scale-out)\nNet weight = gross - tare
    Unloading --> OnHold : Unloading incident raised

    %% ── QC & completion ────────────────────────────
    ScaleOut --> QCPending : Scale-out complete; gate pass issued\n(QC event auto-created)

    QCPending --> Completed : QC inspection passed\n(trip cost calculation triggered)
    QCPending --> OnHold : QC failure — re-inspection required

    %% ── Cross-cutting: OnHold ──────────────────────
    OnHold --> Assigned : Hold resolved — back to pre-dispatch
    OnHold --> Loading : Hold resolved — resume loading
    OnHold --> InTransit : Hold resolved — resume transit
    OnHold --> Unloading : Hold resolved — resume unloading
    OnHold --> QCPending : Re-inspection scheduled
    OnHold --> Cancelled : Irresolvable — trip cancelled

    %% ── Terminal states ────────────────────────────
    Completed --> [*] : Trip cost record created\n→ Vendor invoice generated
    Cancelled --> [*] : Cancellation reason recorded

    %% ── State notes ────────────────────────────────
    note right of Pending
        Initial state on TO creation.
        Awaiting vehicle + driver assignment.
    end note

    note right of GateIn
        Gate operator logs vehicle_registration,
        party_type, and entry_time.
        Triggers scale-in queue.
    end note

    note right of ScaleIn
        Tare weight (empty vehicle) captured
        at origin weighbridge.
        Used for net weight calculation at destination.
    end note

    note right of InTransit
        Real-time GPS tracking active (60s interval).
        Route deviation alerts may trigger OnHold.
    end note

    note right of ScaleOut
        Net weight = gross_weight_kg − tare_weight_kg.
        gate_pass_token generated and attached
        to GatePass record.
    end note

    note right of QCPending
        QC event auto-created on ScaleOutComplete event.
        QC inspector performs physical/lab inspection.
        Pass → Completed; Fail → OnHold (re-inspection).
    end note

    note right of Completed
        Final state. Triggers:
        1. TripCost calculation (Celery task)
        2. VendorInvoice generation
        3. ERP sync (if configured)
    end note
